      {"name": "tdm", "line": 19, "header": true, "above": ["# tdm.bt -- team deathmatch: find the other team and fight it.", "#", "# Words: core/vocab.h. Grammar: core/bt.h. How to read it:", "#   - The top `pick` is a PRIORITY LIST (trait `none`, factors far apart):", "#     it looks again every second, and at once when something happens (an", "#     enemy comes into sight, the first round of a burst lands).", "#   - Each `tree tdm_...` under it is a WEIGHED choice: an option is worth", "#     its score (the situation, 0..1) x the bot's own weight for the trait", "#     named x the factor x a little luck. So twelve bots with one tree do", "#     twelve things. An option's score must be 0 when it cannot be done.", "#   - With nothing else to do a bot goes to the ENEMY'S BASE (`seek`).", "#   - A bot HAS A ROLE (`tree tdm_duty`): a camper, or not. It is drawn by", "#     lot, once for each bot (`pick roll=once`), and kept in every life:", "#     a camper goes up to a perch and waits there, again and again; it", "#     fights, takes cover and looks into noises as anybody (all that is", "#     above its role in the list), and then goes back up. Rifles and smgs", "#     only: a shotgun is never one.", ""], "root":
